index de13245..4507cbe 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -192,4 +192,27 @@ The project is primarily an exploration of a classic scheduling question:
 
 When several tasks are ready, which one should be executed now in order to improve the schedule as a whole?
 
-Rather than using a fixed greedy rule, the system combines dependency-graph structure with the current execution state to make that decision dynamically.
\ No newline at end of file
+Rather than using a fixed greedy rule, the system combines dependency-graph structure with the current execution state to make that decision dynamically.
+
+Configuration and Experiments
+
+All scoring weights, lookahead variants (including a rollout lookahead) and event-handling options are exposed through backend.SchedulerConfig; SchedulerConfig.DEFAULT reproduces the original scheduler exactly (verified by GoldenTraceTest).
+
+Reproducible benchmark experiments: benchmark.ExperimentRunner (instances from benchmark.InstanceGenerator, exact optima from benchmark.ExactSolver). Results and methodology are documented in PHASE1_REPORT.md.
+
+Optimized Presets (Phase 2)
+
+Three opt-in presets are available; SchedulerConfig.DEFAULT is unchanged and remains the default.
+
+SchedulerConfig.PHASE1_ROLLOUT: the Phase 1 rollout configuration with the original weights.
+SchedulerConfig.FAST_OPTIMIZED: no lookahead, learned weights; about 2x faster than the original, makespan GM 0.9907 vs original on the 4,500-instance test set (quality equal to plain critical-path-first).
+SchedulerConfig.QUALITY_OPTIMIZED: the rollout with learned weights; makespan GM 0.9885 vs original and 0.9986 vs PHASE1_ROLLOUT on the same test set, at about 1x the original's single-thread runtime on 10-30-task graphs, 4-7x on 31-600-task graphs and about 29x on 601-1,500-task graphs.
+
+Usage: new Controller(tasks, workerNames, printShutdownSummary, SchedulerConfig.QUALITY_OPTIMIZED).
+
+Methodology, all results and limitations are in PHASE2_REPORT.md. To reproduce the optimization (about 4 hours on 12 threads; each stage resumes from target/phase2/run1/evaluations.csv):
+
+mvn -o compile
+java -Xmx4g -cp target/classes benchmark.WeightOptimizer <stage> target/phase2/run1 12
+
+with <stage> in order: datasets, sobol, trackA, raceA, trackB, raceB, validation, test, timing, reproduce. The test stage refuses to run a second time in the same directory.
